-- title:
--   Divisorial presentation of a Pic⁰-point on the regular model
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$, a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak P$ of level $N_0p$ over $R =$ `DRLevel.R p`, and a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation $D$ for the structure morphism `DRLevel.toBase N₀ p` (a scheme with a morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} R$ split by a zero section), together with data $hD$ exhibiting $D$ as representing the condition `algEquivZeroCut` on line bundles rigidified along $\mathfrak P.\varepsilon_{\inf}$ — bundles whose fibres over algebraically closed points are algebraically equivalent to zero — so that $hD$ supplies a Poincaré bundle on $D$ together with its universal property. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O : R \to O$ and maximal ideal generated by $p$, $K$ its fraction field, $\kappa$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with $O \to \kappa$, and let $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ be a resolved model package `DRResolvedModelPackageLevel N₀ p 𝔓 O ρO κ toκ`: an integral, locally Noetherian, proper flat $O$-scheme $Y$ with a proper morphism $\mathrm{toDR}$ to the base change of the Deligne–Rapoport model along $\rho_O$, regular with stalks of Krull dimension at most $2$ outside the fibre over $p$, isomorphic to the model over the smooth locus and over the generic fibre, and with invertible integral component ideal sheaves $\mathrm{comp}(F)$, indexed by $F \in$ `X0MqComponents 𝔛reg.width`, whose product cuts out $(p)$. Let $z$ be an $O$-point of $D$ over $\rho_O$, let $\sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_m$ be sections of $Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$, let $\mathrm{pos}, \mathrm{neg} : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathbb N$, and let $v_j$ be components such that the image of the closed point of $O$ under $\sigma_j$ lies in the support of $\mathrm{comp}(v_j)$ and in the support of no other component. Assume that the restriction to $Y_K$ of the $\mathrm{toDR}$-pullback of the line bundle $(hD.\mathrm{poincare}.\mathrm{pullbackAlong}\ z).L$ is isomorphic to the iterated tensor product, folded over $j$, of `sectionTwist` of $\sigma_j$ in degree $\mathrm{pos}_j$ — the dual of the $\mathrm{pos}_j$-th power of the ideal sheaf of the section — tensored with the module of the $\mathrm{neg}_j$-th power of that ideal sheaf, with unit at the end. Then there exist $a^+, a^- :$ `X0MqComponents 𝔛reg.width` $\to \mathbb N$ such that the $\mathrm{toDR}$-pullback of $(hD.\mathrm{poincare}.\mathrm{pullbackAlong}\ z).L$ to $Y$ is isomorphic to the fold over $j$ of $(\ker \sigma_j^{\mathrm{pos}_j})^{\vee} \otimes \ker \sigma_j^{\mathrm{neg}_j} \otimes (-)$, applied to $(\prod_F \mathrm{comp}(F)^{a^+_F})^{\vee} \otimes \prod_F \mathrm{comp}(F)^{a^-_F}$, where $\ker \sigma_j$ denotes the kernel ideal sheaf of the section and $(-)^{\vee}$ the dual module.
--
--   This is the extension step from the generic fibre to the regular model: a rigidified line bundle in the algebraic-equivalence-zero part of the relative Picard functor, whose generic fibre is presented by a divisor supported on sections, admits on the regular model a presentation by the same sections corrected by an integral combination of the components of the special fibre. It feeds the multidegree computation [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackageLevel.multidegree_mem_range_intersectionAlpha_of_pullbackAlong_generic_iso_of_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackageLevel.multidegree_mem_range_intersectionAlpha_of_pullbackAlong_generic_iso_of_surjective), where the component coefficients are paired with the intersection matrix of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0p)$.
